{"n": 1306, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "1306.webp", "text": "BODY CAVITY SEALING — ‘3’ SERIES — E 30\nSealing Preparations Sealing Procedures on Lifting Platform\n\n(wheels protected with covers available from HWB)\n~ Underside of car must be clean and dry.\n\n1. Front cross member, through openings on sides H or F\n— If applicable, damaged PVC on underside including wheel housings and side panels\nmust be repaired and treated with Tectyl. 2. Side panels and wheel housings - front N of RS\nThe thickness of undercoating should not exceed 250 yum (0.25 mm / 0.010\"), 3. Engine carrier over entire length Nor RS\n~ Check car for paint finish damage and damage from flying stones and, if applicable, 4. Front side panels in rear area from behind through provided hole Nor RS\nrepair after consulting the customer.\n5. All reinforcement of floor assembly in front seat area through provided Nor RS\n— Sealing Speers and the car itself should have room temperature openings\n(approx, Cc / 68° F).\n6. Door member at center from underneath Nor AS\n~ Check spray pattern of guns and nozzles.\nmn 5 7. Doors twice each through provided holes as well as front door window T+N of F+RS\n— When drilling holes, dip the stepped drill bit in sealing compound to trap burrs. frame at rear (plates removed)\n— Remove dripping sealing compound. 8. Left and right rear spring mounts through provided openings N or RS\n— Insert plugs dipped in Tecty! in all drilled holes after finishing sealing. 9. Side and cross members underneath trunk through provided openings Nor RS\n\n— Spray engine sealing compound on engine and engine compartment to cover\n\ncompletely. ing Procedures without Lifting Platform\n— When repairing body parts damaged in an accident or replacing the car body, 10. Braces of engine hood and all member sections of front panel through Hof F\nbody cavity seating must be carried out immediately after painting and before provided openings\ninstallation of attachments, equipment, trim, etc.. If repair welding seams and\njoints are only accessible from one side, the side which produces a cavity has 11. Spring strut peak reinforcement HorF\nto be treated with wax. The same is applicable for the rear side panels, above\nthe wheel housings up to the roof joint, as well as doors especially in the upper 12. Wheel house braces / cowl panel from underneath H#N or F+RS\ncorner areas.\n13. A pillar (door contact switches removed; cars with radio: speakers Nor RS\nremoved)\nBody cavity sealing performed after body repairs must be confirmed 14, Rear side panels and wheel housing through rubber rubbing strip N or RS\n‘on the annual inspection sheets (Owner’s Manual) ! openings (2-door cars) or door member/rear side panel joints (4-door cars)\n15. Rear side panels and wheel housings from trunk NorRS\n16. Braces of trunk lid through provided openings Hor F\n\nH = Hook-type probe\n\nN = Nylon probe\n\nT =Door probe\n\nRS = Round spray pattern slotted nozzle\nF = Flat spray pattern nozzle", "words": [["BODY", 0.3799, 0.0623, 0.4108, 0.0736], ["CAVITY", 0.4149, 0.0623, 0.4574, 0.0736], ["SEALING", 0.461, 0.063, 0.5096, 0.0743], ["—", 0.5142, 0.069, 0.5208, 0.071], ["‘3’", 0.5253, 0.063, 0.537, 0.0743], ["SERIES", 0.54, 0.0623, 0.58, 0.0743], ["—", 0.5836, 0.0683, 0.5907, 0.0703], ["E", 0.5947, 0.063, 0.6008, 0.0736], ["30", 0.6054, 0.063, 0.617, 0.0736], ["Sealing", 0.0147, 0.0942, 0.0502, 0.1074], ["Preparations", 0.0537, 0.0942, 0.1125, 0.1074], ["Sealing", 0.5091, 0.0962, 0.5431, 0.1101], ["Procedures", 0.5466, 0.0955, 0.5993, 0.1074], ["on", 0.6028, 0.0988, 0.615, 0.1068], ["Lifting", 0.619, 0.0955, 0.651, 0.1094], ["Platform", 0.6545, 0.0955, 0.696, 0.1074], ["(wheels", 0.5096, 0.1127, 0.5451, 0.124], ["protected", 0.5486, 0.1127, 0.5952, 0.1253], ["with", 0.5988, 0.1121, 0.6201, 0.1233], ["covers", 0.6231, 0.1147, 0.653, 0.1233], ["available", 0.656, 0.1121, 0.6971, 0.1233], ["from", 0.7006, 0.1121, 0.7244, 0.1227], ["HWB)", 0.728, 0.1114, 0.7558, 0.1233], ["~", 0